{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfkG7a62ibsCZRCYt51Wt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate for this exploratory slot, and it passes the admission self-check (`OK`). It will almost certainly lose to the current models, though: its quick-check ELPD-LOO was −4313.6, against −3602.5 for the incumbent `gamblers_second_order_person_lapse`.\n\n**Model name:** `encoding_cost_chunk_parse`\n\n**Hypothesis:** people judge how random a sequence is by how hard it would be to remember. They store it as the cheapest list of chunks, each chunk either a streak of one face or a stretch of strict alternation. A sequence that costs more to store looks more random. An alternating chunk costs a fitted amount compared with a streak chunk, so that cost decides both how a sequence is split into chunks and how random it looks.\n\nThis is a different kind of explanation from the models in the current set, which all weigh a fair coin against regular generators. It extends the pruned Falk & Konold DP model in three ways:\n- **Fitted chunk cost:** the cost of an alternating chunk is fitted, where DP fixes it at twice a streak chunk.\n- **Length scaling:** the remembering cost is divided by a fitted power of the sequence length.\n- **People differ:** each person has their own decisiveness and their own leaning towards the Left or Right button, as a response-stage addition.\n\n**How it's built:** every possible way of splitting each H/T sequence of length 1–8 into chunks is worked out once, when the file loads. Inside the model, the cheapest split is just a minimum over a fixed table, so the likelihood runs over all trials at once with no per-trial loops or scans.\n\n**Self-check:** the file loads, the log-probability is finite, the data contract holds, and a short fit (one chain, 100 draws) has a finite ELPD-LOO. Two warnings came with it:\n- **Unreliable LOO estimate:** 4.0% of trials have Pareto k above 0.5, over the 1% tolerance. The real fit may also be flagged as unreliable.\n- **Convergence not checked:** a one-chain fit can't report R-hat, so convergence and the novelty check will only happen at admission.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_0/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3603,"cache_read_input_tokens":82133,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3603,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e9f4929-43b9-4a0d-92a9-86059469c435","uuid":"1f0a59bf-5417-4be5-b585-a25fc9665425","timestamp":"2026-10-06T03:19:19.377Z","request_id":"req_011CfkG7ZaXPhytUz9WWdv4m"}
